Let condition (0) of the GAC be satisfied relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in a $\mathrm{CPDAG}$ ($\mathrm{PAG}$) $\mathcal{G}$. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
   \begin{itemize}
       \item $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies condition (1) of the GAC relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in $\mathcal{G}$.
       \item $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies condition (a) of the AC relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in every $\mathrm{DAG}$ ($\mathrm{MAG}$) in $[\mathcal{G}]$.
   \end{itemize}

Let condition (0) of the GAC be satisfied relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in a $\mathrm{CPDAG}$ ($\mathrm{PAG}$) $\mathcal{G}$, and let $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfy condition (1) of the GAC relative to  $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in $\mathcal{G}$. Then the following two statements are equivalent:
   \begin{itemize}
      \item $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies condition (2) of the GAC relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in $\mathcal{G}$.
      \item $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies condition (b) of the AC relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in every $\mathrm{DAG}$ ($\mathrm{MAG}$) in $[\mathcal{G}]$.
   \end{itemize}
